<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 February, from 532 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justinian-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">532 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian I begins building the new Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Only weeks after the second basilica was destroyed, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> began the construction of a third, larger church, designed by Anthemius of Tralles and Isidore of Miletus. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a> was completed in 537.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">705 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,321 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wu Zetian abdicates and the Tang dynasty is restored</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a>, the only woman to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> as emperor in her own right, gave up the throne, and her self-styled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a> was abolished in favour of the restored Tang. She had ruled alone since 690.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1455">1455 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">571 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date for the completion of the Gutenberg Bible</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Johannes Gutenberg</a>'s Bible was completed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> around this date. It was the first major book printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> with movable metal type, and print spread rapidly across the continent.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Johannes Gutenberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1685">1685 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">341 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Frideric Handel is born in Halle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Handel trained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> before settling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, where he wrote operas, the 'Water Music' and the oratorio 'Messiah'. He became a naturalised British subject in 1727.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1836">1836 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Siege of the Alamo begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Santa Anna's Mexican army surrounded the Texian garrison in the Alamo mission at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a>. After thirteen days the defenders, including Jim Bowie and Davy Crockett, were killed in the final assault.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln arrives secretly in Washington</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warned of a plot to kill him in Baltimore, President-elect Lincoln travelled through the city overnight in secret. He was mocked for the manner of his arrival, ten days before his inauguration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rotary Club founded in Chicago</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lawyer Paul Harris and three business acquaintances met to found the first Rotary Club. Rotary International now has some 1.4 million members and led the campaign to eradicate polio.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines raise the flag on Mount Suribachi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marines planted the US flag on the summit of Iwo Jima's volcano. Joe Rosenthal's photograph of the second, larger flag won the Pulitzer Prize, though the fighting went on for another month.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 23 February <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-paul-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Paul II</span><span class="tp">1417–1471</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis IX, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1417–1479</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/matthias-corvinus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Matthias Corvinus</span><span class="tp">1443–1490</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/samuel-pepys"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/samuel-pepys.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Samuel Pepys</span><span class="tp">1633–1703</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-le-moyne-de-bienville"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-baptiste-le-moyne-de-bienville.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean-Baptiste Le Moyne de Bienville</span><span class="tp">1680–1767</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-frideric-handel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Frideric Handel</span><span class="tp">1685–1759</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 23 February <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/li-keyong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/li-keyong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Li Keyong</span><span class="tp">856–908</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/herbert-ii-count-of-vermandois"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/herbert-ii-count-of-vermandois.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Herbert II, Count of Vermandois</span><span class="tp">c. 880–943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-eugene-iv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-eugene-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Eugene IV</span><span class="tp">1383–1447</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zhengtong-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Zhengtong Emperor</span><span class="tp">1427–1464</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-columbus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Diego Columbus</span><span class="tp">c. 1479–1526</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stanislaw-leszczynski.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stanisław Leszczyński</span><span class="tp">1677–1766</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolphus-frederick-vi-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-strelitz"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Adolphus Frederick VI, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</span><span class="tp">1882–1918</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tomoyuki-yamashita"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tomoyuki-yamashita.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tomoyuki Yamashita</span><span class="tp">1885–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-napoleon-duarte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-napoleon-duarte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Napoleón Duarte</span><span class="tp">1925–1990</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
